Observation: HasId condition converter creates HashSet of segment_ids by mapping external IDs to internal IDs via filter_map (returns None for non-existent IDs). For has_id=[], this creates empty HashSet. The condition_checker returns predicate: point_id => segment_ids.contains(point_id). Empty HashSet means predicate returns false for all point_ids, so filter should match 0 points. Bug not in this code - must be in filter execution or result counting layer.
